    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1646">

                <pb facs="1043" n="927" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg927"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 511.4A1/1470.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2494.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the Netherlands</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to my note
                    No. 2424 of the 12th instant, by which I took leave to announce to your
                    excellency that the Opium Conference would open on June 15 next, I have the
                    honor to inform you that it appears from a communication which I have just
                    received from my Government that the Austro-Hungarian Government which for
                    formal reasons has not yet been able to sign the Convention has declared its
                    adhesion to the contents of the Convention and its readiness to enforce its
                    provisions if the other Governments decide that the Convention may be put into
                    operation.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. L. F. C. de Rappard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
